# work-strategy minds — granular use (tri-mind deprecated)

**`tri-mind` / `tri-frame` / `tutti` are deprecated** — see [TRI-MIND-DEPRECATED.md](../../docs/skill-work/work-strategy/TRI-MIND-DEPRECATED.md). Do **not** run the A/B/C menu or tri-frame roundtables in new sessions.

Do **not** assume **tri-frame** (Mercouris + Mearsheimer + Barnes together) on every **`strategy`**, **`strategy pass`**, **`work-strategy`**, or generic **skill-strategy** / strategy-notebook pass.

**Default:** Use **zero or one** named lens — or **none** (plain Chronicle / Reflection / References without M/M/B labeling). Multi-lens comparison → **[`statecraft-multi-lens`](../../.cursor/skills/statecraft-multi-lens/SKILL.md)**.

**Named mind (single):** When the operator names **Mercouris**, **Mearsheimer**, **Barnes**, or another mapped expert, read that mind's SSOT and render in authentic register per [minds-authentic-voice.mdc](minds-authentic-voice.mdc).

**LEARN MODE** tri-frame ordering is **legacy** — [LEARN_MODE_RULES.md](../../docs/skill-work/work-strategy/LEARN_MODE_RULES.md) applies only when the operator explicitly invokes archive LEARN protocol.

**Entry points:** [`docs/skill-work/work-strategy/minds/README.md`](../../docs/skill-work/work-strategy/minds/README.md) → canonical **`strategy-notebook/minds/CIV-MIND-*.md`** (full mind bodies in-repo; **no civ-mem required**). Optional upstream diff: `research/repos/civilization_memory/docs/templates/CIV–MIND–*.md` when present.

**In-voice output:** When a **single** named mind is invoked, follow [`.cursor/rules/minds-authentic-voice.mdc`](minds-authentic-voice.mdc) (read fingerprints; no neutral substitute for authentic register).
